package skill

// One contract for schema and analyzer teaching; examples do not route or gate.
const AnalysisCurrentSourceExplanationTeaching = "current_source_explanation_profile preserves a requested current-source explanation alongside a non-source observation, including a command measurement that will be collected later. Emit is_current_source_explanation_requested=true when the current request asks to explain, verify, trace, compare, locate or assess that observation using the current checkout. This secondary dimension survives a count/return_value primary intent and does not require an attached artifact. Use modes from the schema and verbatim source_quotes; optional target_terms guide search, not evidence. Source scope, risk flags and current_source_mode=allow do not replace this profile. Artifact citations or unmapped frames do not cancel requested source analysis. For artifact-only summaries or ordinary code-only questions leave it inactive. It is soft guidance, not a hard answer gate; unanchored quotes warn rather than retry. External observations default to mixed external + current-source analysis; only anchored explicit source exclusions disable that lane."
